  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fipsen (German solo trick-taker). 3-5 players (optimal 4). 32-card deck (some regions use 36). Bidding: Each player bids 1-8 tricks (highest bidder becomes soloist). Soloist may draw from Skat (optional). Gameplay: 8 tricks total. Lead player starts; others follow suit if able. Scoring: Soloist scores bid amount if they make bid tricks; lose bid amount if fail. Defenders win if soloist fails. Rotate bidder for next round.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Fipsen! Bid for the number of tricks you think you can make (1-8). If you win the bidding, you play solo against the other three players. Make your bid and you score the bid amount; fail and you lose those points. The 7 of Diamonds is specialâ€”watch for it!',
    objective: 'Win the number of tricks declared during the bidding phase. If the bidder succeeds, they win points; if they fail, they are penalized.',
    gameplay: '1. Lead: The bidder leads the first trick.\n2. Following Suit: Players must follow suit if possible.\n3. Trumps: If you cannot follow suit, you may play a trump.',
    keyRules: [
      'Siebener Fips: If a player is dealt all four Sevens (Club, Spade, Heart, and Diamond) plus an Ace, they win immediately and score 30 points.',
      "Doubling: Scoring values double if Clubs are trumps or if a player declares 'Diamonds' (Ruten).",
      "Kloppen: An opponent can 'Knock' (Kloppen) to double the stakes again.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
